{#-
  Shared provider-tooling block. `is_github` is provided by the lmer renderer
  (see taskdef/README.md). When it is unset or false — e.g. an lmer version that
  predates GitHub support and does not pass it — the GitLab instructions render,
  matching historical behavior.
-#}
{% if is_github -%}
This repository is hosted on **GitHub** (`{{ LMER_REPO_HOST }}`).

- Use **`github-review`** for atomic inline reviews (`--review-file`) and normalized reads (`--info`, `--issue-info`, `--comments`, `--all-comments`, `--list`).
- `--resolve-thread` is a mutation reserved for review contexts: only a review session (or a human) resolves a thread, after verifying the fix — fix authors reply and leave threads open (Thread Resolution Policy, rules/git.md).
- Use **`gh`** directly for create-PR, create-issue, comment, edit, and close — these are intentionally not wrapped.
- Run `bash /Agents/global/hooks/github-review-docs.sh` to familiarize yourself with the tool.
- A 404 / auth failure during `github-review` or `gh` usually means a missing or invalid token — check the env for `GH_TOKEN`, `GITHUB_TOKEN`, or a per-host `GH_TOKEN_<host>` variable.
{%- else -%}
This repository is hosted on **GitLab**{% if LMER_REPO_HOST is defined and LMER_REPO_HOST %} (`{{ LMER_REPO_HOST }}`){% endif %}.

- Use **`gitlab-review`** for merge-request and issue operations.
- `--resolve-thread` is a mutation reserved for review contexts: only a review session (or a human) resolves a thread, after verifying the fix — fix authors reply and leave threads open (Thread Resolution Policy, rules/git.md).
- Run `bash /Agents/global/hooks/gitlab-review-docs.sh` to familiarize yourself with the tool.
- A 404 during `gitlab-review` may indicate an invalid token — check the env for `_TOKEN` variables to see if there are multiple GitLab tokens specified.
{%- endif %}
